      "Choose Today for work scheduled on the current Asia/Kolkata calendar date; future work is excluded. Overall includes earlier, today, future and undated work, and completed work when its status permits. FMS opens in Overall by default so assigned work without a deadline or scheduled ahead stays visible. Other subsections open in Today by default. A date scope you explicitly select stays selected across categories; counts and drilldowns use the same server scope. Overdue lists unfinished work scheduled before today.",
      "See my tasks: open Tasks. My Tasks lists recurring work; Delegated lists one-time assigned work for employees; In Loop lists watched work. Open the FMS subsection for your assigned workflow work, grouped by workflow family and published stage. Subsection counts load when Tasks opens using each destination tab's date scope and authorized team scope. Loading counts are not shown as zero; the FMS subsection count covers the whole workspace, while board and search counts describe their filtered results.",
      "Do an anytime duty: work without a fixed time (As Required, Per Customer, After Visit and similar) is under the \"Anytime duties\" bar at the top of My Tasks (Pending); the bar is closed until you tap it. They are low priority with no deadline and come back every day. Press \"Start\" whenever you do one; it opens as a low-priority task due tonight, and it also appears in your task list (marked \"Anytime duty\") so you can finish it later. Complete it like any other task (upload, checklist, form). Press \"Continue\" to finish one already open. You can do the same duty several times a day. If a manager assigns one, it appears in your list as a high-priority task.",
      "Half-day deadlines: the day has two fixed deadlines, First half at 3:00 PM and Second half at 9:00 PM (India time). Work that has no due date of its own (a new FMS step whose form gave no date, a start form you were asked to fill, a CRM walk-in task, a duty a manager assigns without a time) gets one when it reaches you: before 3:00 PM it is due 9:00 PM the same day; from 3:00 PM on it is due 3:00 PM the next day. Weekends and holidays are not skipped. A due time of 3:00 PM or 9:00 PM shows \"First half\" or \"Second half\" next to it. When it passes, the task is overdue like any other.",
      "Task order: My Tasks shows the earliest due date first; tasks due at the same time show high priority before medium and low. Overdue shows the longest overdue first; Completed shows the most recent first.",
